Create the SettingsSidebar Blazor component at `/tmp/sv-9cd8dbbeca7248e59f40b2e490fb581b/Components/Pages/Settings/SettingsSidebar.razor` and its CSS isolation file.

This is a vertical navigation sidebar for a settings dashboard. It has four sections: "Profile", "Notifications", "Security", "Appearance". The active section is highlighted. Clicking a section fires a callback.

**Parameters:**
- `[Parameter] public string ActiveSection { get; set; }` — the currently active section name
- `[Parameter] public EventCallback<string> OnSectionChanged { get; set; }` — fired when user clicks a section

**Markup:**
- A `<nav>` with CSS class `settings-sidebar`
- Each item is a `<button>` with class `sidebar-item` (and additional class `active` when it matches ActiveSection)
- Each button shows an icon (use Bootstrap Icons unicode or simple emoji/text icons) and the section name
- Use `@onclick` to fire `OnSectionChanged` with the section name

**CSS isolation file** (`SettingsSidebar.razor.css`):
```css
.settings-sidebar {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    min-width: 220px;
    background-color: #f8f9fa;
    border-right: 1px solid #dee2e6;
    height: 100%;
}

.sidebar-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    border: none;
    background: none;
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #495057;
    text-align: left;
    transition: background-color 0.15s, color 0.15s;
}

.sidebar-item:hover {
    background-color: #e9ecef;
}

.sidebar-item.active {
    background-color: #0d6efd;
    color: white;
    font-weight: 600;
}

.sidebar-icon {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    width: 1.5rem;
    text-align: center;
}
```

Use the `create` tool to create both files. Do NOT use `@rendermode` on this component — it inherits from parent.

Create the ProfileSection Blazor component at `/tmp/sv-9cd8dbbeca7248e59f40b2e490fb581b/Components/Pages/Settings/ProfileSection.razor` and its CSS isolation file.

This component lets users edit their profile. It injects `ISettingsService` to load/save data.

**Namespace context:** The project namespace is `sv_9cd8dbbeca7248e59f40b2e490fb581b`. The service interface is:
```csharp
public record UserProfile(string DisplayName, string Email, string AvatarUrl, string Bio);
public interface ISettingsService {
    Task<UserProfile> GetProfileAsync();
    Task SaveProfileAsync(UserProfile profile);
    // ...other methods
}
```

**Behavior:**
- On `OnInitializedAsync`, load the profile via `ISettingsService.GetProfileAsync()`
- Store the loaded profile as `savedProfile` (the last saved state) and create a mutable copy for editing (use individual fields: `displayName`, `email`, `avatarUrl`, `bio`)
- Show a loading spinner while data loads
- Show a success message (a simple div with class `alert alert-success`) for 3 seconds after saving. Use a `successMessage` string field and a `CancellationTokenSource` to manage the timer. Implement `IAsyncDisposable` to cancel the timer on disposal.

**Markup (use Bootstrap classes):**
- Wrapper div with class `settings-section`
- `<h3>Profile Settings</h3>`
- Avatar preview area: a div with class `avatar-preview` containing an `<img>` tag showing the avatarUrl (or a placeholder div if empty), plus a text input for the avatar URL below it
- Form fields using Bootstrap `form-group` / `mb-3` classes:
  - Display Name: `<input type="text" class="form-control">`
  - Email: `<input type="email" class="form-control">`
  - Bio: `<textarea class="form-control" rows="4">`
- Button area with two buttons:
  - "Save Changes" (`btn btn-primary`) — calls `SaveProfileAsync` with a new `UserProfile` record, updates `savedProfile`, shows success message
  - "Discard Changes" (`btn btn-outline-secondary`) — reverts fields to `savedProfile` values
- Both buttons disabled while loading
- Track `isSaving` to disable the save button and show "Saving..." text during save

**CSS isolation file** (`ProfileSection.razor.css`):
```css
.settings-section {
    padding: 1.5rem;
}

.avatar-preview {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
}

.avatar-preview img {
    width: 100px;
    height: 100px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 3px solid #dee2e6;
}

.avatar-placeholder {
    width: 100px;
    height: 100px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background-color: #e9ecef;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 2rem;
    color: #6c757d;
    border: 3px solid #dee2e6;
}

.button-group {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
}
```

Use `@inject ISettingsService SettingsService` at the top. Do NOT use `@rendermode`. Use the `create` tool to create both files.

Create the NotificationsSection Blazor component at `/tmp/sv-9cd8dbbeca7248e59f40b2e490fb581b/Components/Pages/Settings/NotificationsSection.razor` and its CSS isolation file.

This component lets users manage notification preferences. It injects `ISettingsService`.

**Namespace context:** The project namespace is `sv_9cd8dbbeca7248e59f40b2e490fb581b`. The relevant types:
```csharp
public record NotificationPrefs(bool EmailNotifications, bool PushNotifications, bool WeeklyDigest, List<string> MutedChannels);
public interface ISettingsService {
    Task<NotificationPrefs> GetNotificationPrefsAsync();
    Task SaveNotificationPrefsAsync(NotificationPrefs prefs);
}
```

**Behavior:**
- On `OnInitializedAsync`, load prefs via `GetNotificationPrefsAsync()`
- Store mutable copies: `emailNotifications`, `pushNotifications`, `weeklyDigest` (bool fields), and `mutedChannels` (List<string>)
- The available channels list is hardcoded: `"general"`, `"announcements"`, `"updates"`, `"marketing"`, `"alerts"`
- A channel is "muted" if it appears in `mutedChannels`
- Show loading state, success message on save (same pattern as profile: `alert alert-success` div shown for 3 seconds, use CancellationTokenSource, implement IAsyncDisposable)

**Markup (Bootstrap classes):**
- Wrapper div `settings-section`
- `<h3>Notification Preferences</h3>`
